  <title>The Properties panel</title>

  <p>The <gui>Properties</gui> panel, beside the canvas, shows whatever is
  selected and changes it. Every change applies as you make it, and the
  canvas redraws as you type.</p>

  <section id="rows">
    <title>What it shows</title>
    <list>
      <item><p>At the top, what is selected: the kind of element, such as
      <gui>Frame</gui>, or <gui>Group of 3</gui>, or <gui>3 elements</gui>.</p></item>
      <item><p><gui>X</gui> and <gui>Y</gui>, the left and top of the
      selection in dots. Typing a new value moves the whole
      selection.</p></item>
      <item><p><gui>Print This Element</gui>. Clear it to keep the selection
      off the printed label while keeping it in the design.</p></item>
      <item><p>For one element, all of its own settings: the pages under
      <link xref="index#elements">What goes on a label</link> describe
      each kind's.</p></item>
      <item><p>For several elements, only the settings they all have, such
      as <gui>Thickness</gui> for frames and circles or <gui>Font
      Height</gui> for text. A value they do not share reads
      <gui>Mixed</gui>, and a value you type is given to every one of
      them. Text, barcode data and the like are each element's own:
      <key>Ctrl</key>-click one element to change those.</p></item>
    </list>
  </section>

  <section id="undo">
    <title>Undo and Escape</title>
    <p>A run of changes in the panel is one step for <gui>Undo</gui>. It ends
    when you press <key>Enter</key>, leave the panel, pause for a second, or
    select something else. <key>Escape</key> throws away the run you are in
    the middle of.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="dock">
    <title>Show, hide and float it</title>
    <p>The panel is docked on the right of the window, and can be pulled off
    to float in a window of its own, then docked again: in the Qt frontend
    by its title bar, in the GTK frontend by the button in its own
    header.</p>
    <p>Docked, it always shows the selection. Floating, it stays away until
    you ask for it, and then follows the selection until you close it. Bring
    it back with any of:</p>
    <list>
      <item><p>a double click on an element</p></item>
      <item><p><guiseq><gui>Edit</gui><gui>Properties</gui></guiseq> or
      <gui>Properties</gui> in the right-click menu
      (<keyseq><key>Alt</key><key>Enter</key></keyseq>)</p></item>
      <item><p><guiseq><gui>View</gui><gui>Properties Panel</gui></guiseq></p></item>
    </list>
    <p>Its size and whether it floats are remembered.</p>
  </section>
</page>
